.TH MU2E_SEND 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-dataformat-viewer t01.00.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2e_send \- send raw packet bytes to the data format viewer over TCP or UDP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2e_send
.RB [ \-u | \-\-udp ]
.I host port hex-byte
.RI [ hex-byte ...]
.br
.B mu2e_send
.RB [ \-u | \-\-udp ]
.B \-f
.I file host port
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends the given bytes as one TCP connection (connect, send all, close) or one
UDP datagram, using
.BR libmu2e_sender (3).
Bytes are taken from the arguments, each a hex value 0\(en0xFF with an
optional
.B 0x
prefix, or from a binary file.
Options must precede
.I host
and
.IR port .
.PP
Built from
.I cpp/
with CMake; it is not built or installed by the Python bootstrap.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-udp
UDP instead of TCP.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIFILE\fR"
Read the payload from
.IR FILE ;
no hex arguments may follow.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a usage error, unreadable file, empty payload or send
failure.
A TCP peer that closes early can terminate the program with SIGPIPE.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
cmake \-S cpp \-B cpp/build \-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake \-\-build cpp/build
cpp/build/mu2e_send localhost 7755 00 10 80 10 cd ef 00 ab 00 00 00 01 a0 20 00 00
cpp/build/mu2e_send \-\-udp \-f test/test.dat localhost 7755
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmu2e_sender (3),
.BR mu2edaq\-dataformat\-viewer.py (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e DAQ group, Fermilab.
